<item><title>Mauritania weighs border risks after UN ends MINURSO mandate</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-weighs-border-risks-after-un-ends-minurso-mandate-19cbbb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-weighs-border-risks-after-un-ends-minurso-mandate-19cbbb/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>The Security Council declined to renew the Western Sahara mission on 30 October, removing a mechanism that monitored incidents and helped contain escalation.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:20:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
